# SAME70Q20B USB-CDC boot/connect smoke test. Exercises the
# CONFIG_ATSAM_USB firmware variant (duet3-6hc / duet3-6xd printer
# configs are USB+CAN-only on real hardware, no serial-mode firmware
# variant exists) against the local USBHS Renode peripheral
# (test/emulator/repl/same70_usbhs.cs). The peripheral uses a
# "skip-enum cheat" - inject a SET_CONFIGURATION SETUP packet on EP0
# so klipper's CDC stack reaches bulk-active without a full USB host
# emulation - then exposes BULK_IN/BULK_OUT as a UART pipe to the
# host pty via UARTBase. The companion same70_smoke.test covers the
# CONFIG_ATSAM_SERIAL path; both share the same .repl (USBHS is
# resident unconditionally and stays idle when the firmware never
# touches it).
#
# KNOWN BLOCKED (the "44th" test in the PR summary). The skip-enum
# cheat works far enough that klippy completes identify ("Loaded MCU
# 'mcu' 132 commands"), but _send_get_config then sees is_shutdown=1
# and raises. Diagnosis (refined this round; run with
# RENODE_PEEK_SHUTDOWN=1 to surface it - the launcher logs "FIRMWARE
# SHUTDOWN reason=N"):
#   * The firmware shuts down with static_string_id 56, "Rescheduled
#     timer in the past" (armcm_timer.c timer_dispatch_many: the next
#     timer is >1ms behind DWT->CYCCNT).
#   * It is USB-build specific: same70_smoke (serial) never shuts down,
#     and a no-enumeration A/B (suppressing the SETUP injection so no
#     klippy traffic flows) still shuts down - so the cause is the
#     USB-build boot/main-loop, not klippy traffic or the cheat itself.
#   * It is a CPU-rate / DWT-overshoot effect, NOT the systickFrequency
#     mismatch the earlier hypothesis blamed: 450MHz systick vs 300MHz
#     DWT fires the SysTick one-shot EARLY (-> harmless busy-wait), not
#     late. Raising the Renode CPU rate (RENODE_EXP_MIPS=1000) makes
#     the overshoot disappear - but then USB enumeration no longer
#     completes (klippy: "Wait for identify_response" -> connection
#     closed). So there is a real timing tension: the rate that avoids
#     the timer overshoot breaks the USBHS enumeration timing, and vice
#     versa. No single RENODE_EXP_MIPS / SetGlobalQuantum value tried
#     satisfies both; closing this needs the USBHS model's enumeration
#     made robust across CPU rates (or deterministic tick-mode on ARM,
#     which currently mis-frames identify).
DICTIONARY same70q20b-usb.dict
CONFIG same70_usb_smoke.cfg
EMULATOR same70_usb_smoke.fixture.json

# A few harmless gcode lines so klippy gets past klippy:ready.
M114
M105
M105
M105

# klippy connected and stayed connected long enough to do the
# clocksync handshake against the firmware's generic/armcm_timer view
# transported over the synthetic USBHS bulk endpoints.
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Klippy is shutdown"
